WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:05.060
Hello, and welcome to the 2013 Project for Awesome. 
Waaaaaa..!

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:06.640
Hank, are you there or is it just Bobble John?

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.160
It's just Bobble John. My head came off!

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:11.120
Oh no!

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.240
I'm okay, I'm okay.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:13.500
I'm just gonna let this happen.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.900
Continue what you were saying, please. 
Let me put this hat on.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.860
Ladies and gentlemen, my insane brother.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.220
Michael is editing you scooping the brains out of a squirrel right now.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.080
It is the most disgusting video we have ever done!

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.120
The squirrel needed to see a dentist real bad.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.280
I blame Squirrel-bama.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.800
Oh, that's the sweetest wrestling I've ever seen.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.400
I am bigger than you.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.540
I know! Just let me take control!

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.620
Am I gonna hula for you? Good...good question!

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.260
Here's a good answer: no.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:45.420
Put sharpies in my nose.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:46.940
You get to work every morning at 6 o' clock?

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:48.380
I do!

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.700
Do you want to come work for me because you could literally sleep in three extra hours every day.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:53.320
Yes.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:54.660
Do you see it?

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:55.900
I'm having a religious moment.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:57.760
I think his name is Jeff the Buttdog.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:00:59.480
Aghshjgsguaghjahagashuiah!

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:02.988
I'm in a dark wall, I can't go...and there is nowhere to...

00:01:02.988 --> 00:01:04.120
I don't like it!

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.200
This has been an interesting couple of minutes!

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:10.460
I'm concerned that the patriarchy might not even survive to the end of the Project for Awesome.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.980
Just kidding! Just kidding, it's deeply entrenched.

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:16.840
We're adding a new perk right now, and I'm wearing it.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:19.680
Well first of all, he's a smaller man than I am.

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:22.300
This is...not what it looks like on Alex.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:26.200
The number of people watching this just sharply decreased, so... I don't know how to take that.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.180
How do you make a cat look like Benedict Cumberbatch?

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:30.240
Well, blue scarf, right?

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:33.500
I CAME IN LIKE A WRECKING BALL

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:36.960
Make that clearer, not more confusing. Like, the quark model clears things up, amazingly.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:41.760
No!

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:46.100
Oh...

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:52.140
Just so that I can sit there and have the authentic experience of properly eating salami.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:59.340
This is my first ever spoken word piece. 
It's called "Bullies."

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:01.375
Why are you doing pelvic thrusts?

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:02.860
Because you told me to tap dance!

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.900
My hair is everything!

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:12.900
How did you so precisely get your eyes?

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:14.200
I've been practicing!

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.800
It will look like this except it won't already be on cardboard.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:20.680
It will just be, y'know, just a poster that you can roll and unroll, but it'll look like this.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:25.420
What is my Sharpie face removal plan?

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:30.280
Why didn't I think about this before I started to cover my face in Sharpie?

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:37.380
Shorty had them apple bottom jeans and boots with the fur. The whole club was a-lookin' at her!

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:38.800
Three, two, one.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:40.800
Zoom in, zoom in!

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.340
Now we're looking at my blood move.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:45.860
We just raised $525,000!

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:48.540
This is my favorite time of year to be a Nerdfighter,

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:51.880
and it's when I'm proudest of the Nerdfighter community because I get to see the work that we do together.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:55.280
I know that it's hard to take me seriously when I'm covered, still slightly covered, in Sharpie.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.600
I feel you, bro.  
And thanks for getting me into this mess.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:00.620
The Project for Awesome Indiegogo page is open for another 36-ish hours.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:02.600
You can still get all kinds of amazing things there!

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:05.520
My Christmas album, John's sneak peek of the new thing that he's writing,

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:09.380
Project for Awesome t-shirts, posters, commemorative coins, men and women of YouTube charity calendars,

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:15.020
Michael Aranda's actual headshots from when he was 15 years old, and my fake headshot from when I was 8.

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:18.560
Also, yes, The Fault in Our Stars has a movie poster, and this is the only way that you could get it.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:21.180
So, if you want to get that, it's only 25 bucks.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:22.920
And it's all for charity! It's a donation!

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.420
All I gotta say is thank you.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:29.280
Thank you to everybody who commented, who watched the livestream, who made a video, who donated money.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.380
Thanks to everybody who came and joined us on the live show and who participated,

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:33.180
and the men and women of YouTube charity calendars.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:35.440
And of course, thanks to our amazing volunteer support staff,

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:38.720
who stayed up all hours of the day and night with us.

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:40.840
Thanks to Michael Aranda, who designed the poster and the t-shirt.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:43.080
Thanks to Karen Kavett, who designed the calendar and the website.

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:46.680
And thanks to our web developer, Sam Rudge, and Fastly, our hosting service who did it for free.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:50.860
This really is one of my favorite parts of my life, 
so thank you all for being so great.

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:52.120
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

